      "callEndedTimestamp": null,
      "isPinned": false,
      "content": "All on a mature node of the late 1990s? You could have landed that money on a full GF180 MPW shuttle, if considering the minimum price you could have paid (~$20000, for 10x 0p5x0p5 bare die at early bird, which isn't even possible as there are just 9 of those), but you instead chose to buy 10 wafer.space slots where, even if you purchased at least a full slot, that 12.92mm^2 of silicon wouldn't handle most of the stuff mentioned. Other than potentially the linear voltage regulator Tholin mentioned.",
